.\"
.\" PMAP_STATS(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH PMAP_STATS 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
pmap_stats \- get virtual memory statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/pmap.h>
.PP
.BI "int pmap_stats(struct pmap_stats *" stats ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pmap_stats ()
is a Substrate-specific system call that retrieves virtual memory
management statistics into the buffer pointed to by
.IR stats .
.SS The pmap_stats structure
.nf
struct pmap_stats {
    uint32_t page_faults;         /* Total page faults */
    uint32_t cow_duplications;    /* COW page copies made */
    uint32_t cow_pages_mapped;    /* COW pages mapped */
    uint32_t pages_mapped;        /* Total pages mapped */
    uint32_t pages_unmapped;      /* Total pages unmapped */
    uint32_t tlb_shootdowns;      /* TLB invalidations */
};
.fi
.PP
Global statistics can be retrieved by passing a special flag.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned.
.PP
On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I stats
is not a valid pointer.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 241 (SYS_GET_COW_STATS)
Arguments:      stats (on stack)
.fi
.SS Copy-on-Write Monitoring
This syscall is useful for debugging memory usage and monitoring
the effectiveness of copy-on-write after
.BR fork (2)
operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (2),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH HISTORY
Substrate-specific, not available on other Unix systems.
